    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d396">

                <pb facs="0443" n="1121" xml:id="pg1121"/>

                <head>Mr. Pruyn to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 41.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States in
                                Japan</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Yokohama</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-06-24"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 24, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> British indemnity paid. United States
                    legation buildings at Yedo destroyed by fire on the 24th ultimo. Letters
                    received by treaty powers demanding their withdrawal, pursuant to orders of
                    Mikado and Tycoon from Kioto.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, very respectfully, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ROBERT H. PRUYN, <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Resident in
                            Japan.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington.</hi></p>
                    <p>(Above despatch sent to collector, San Francisco, to be telegraphed.)</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
